{"game": "earth-defense-force-5", "language": "english", "appid": 1007040, "month": "2021-10", "window": 2, "start_date": 1633651200, "end_date": 1634342399, "month_true_total": 85, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-28 17:50:57 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "101103724", "author": {"steamid": "76561198004856999", "personaname": "LupusWolf", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/operawuff/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 64, "playtime_forever": 3028, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2812, "last_played": 1636938561, "avatar": "69d91350793fc4f1c9690e1ee269cbcc0550efe2"}, "language": "english", "review": "Punch Godzilla in a giant robot. Punch multiple Godzilla(s) in multiple giant robots. Strap C4 to your allies and launch them at enemies. Beat giant ants to death with anime girl body pilllows. Chant uplifting songs about how all your comrades are dead and the world is a flattened hellscape. Redefine the term Danger Close. Confuse frogs with humans. Reenact that \"Fight in the Shade\" scene from 300, but with wasps instead of Persians. Work with your friends to fight the alien menace. Work against your friends to fight the alien menace. Become the flying panty shot you always wanted to be. But most of all, scream EDF!! while being hurled across the map at high speeds, because morale is important in these trying times.\n\nIt's EDF. Nobody with a pulse hates EDF. It's everything you love about sci-fi B-movies distilled into a fine essence  of explosions and pyrrhic victory. Probably wait on a sale if you aren't a die-hard fan ($60 is probably a bit much), but either way it's a lot of fun.", "timestamp_created": 1634328987, "timestamp_updated": 1634328987, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 15, "votes_funny": 6, "weighted_vote_score": "0.64065861701965332", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primari